# This file has to stand on its own. A global gitignore (core.excludesfile) is per-developer
# machine configuration and is not part of a clone, so anything covered only there is invisible
# to whoever set it up and untracked noise for everyone else. See #63.

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# Windows — the counterpart to the above, and Qud contributors skew Windows
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor / tooling scratch
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Python: tools/ holds the validators, so running them writes tools/__pycache__/.
# README.md tells contributors to run them, so this is generated on a normal first clone.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Node: the repo's XML formatter (prettier + @prettier/plugin-xml) is dev tooling only.
# It lives at the repo root, never in mod/, so it cannot ship to subscribers.
node_modules/

# Claude Code local instructions. CLAUDE.md loads automatically for anyone working in this repo, so
# my personal writing preferences would otherwise be inherited by a contributor's assistant and end
# up shaping their pull requests. The project's own rules are tracked in docs/CHARTER.md,
# docs/LESSONS.md, docs/STYLEGUIDE.md and CONTRIBUTING.md; AGENTS.md points any agent at them.
CLAUDE.md

# Claude Code agent worktrees. Each is a COMPLETE second copy of the working tree, created inside
# the repo and removed when the agent finishes — so it is absent most of the time and present
# exactly while someone is mid-task and least likely to read `git status` closely. Left untracked,
# one `git add -A` stages the whole duplicate.
#
# Only worktrees/, not all of .claude/: a blanket ignore would silently hide agent or skill
# configuration if this project ever checks any in, which is the failure shape this repo keeps
# writing lessons about.
.claude/worktrees/

# Never commit secrets. Nothing here reads a .env today; this is insurance, not a description.
.env

# Qud writes these next to a loaded mod
*.log
